 #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} {:answer/id #uuid "ace51aeb-e1da-564d-aaa1-10285b642108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} :answer-field/id #uuid "72accc2e-3370-511e-9b00-a598c293557b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76850d0b-0e5d-5926-80f5-97253aff4b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103170" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+7)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-3,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-11$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-8$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-7,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-3,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $4,$ i.e., $R\\ge 4.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-11,-3].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-11,-3].$\n\n![](images/47/4764256e5f00e7a11d688bd99d5fa1c22db819e7a188113f0ef4cd987a9b7595.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-11\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $-8\\in (-11,-3],$ the series is convergent at $x=-8.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $1\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
